    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.1. Identifying technically and economically feasible technology and innovation for Hatay, Samandag, in consultation with key stakeholders
1.1.1.1. Stakeholder mapping for Hatay Region
1.1.1.2. Meeting with the relevant stakeholders to introduce the project in Hatay
1.1.1.3. Meeting with relevant parties involving the Japan private sector for exchange of know-how and information
1.1.1.4. Preparation of the feasibility study for technology and innovation for Hatay 
1.1.2. Mapping the application of technologies in Asi river, and Samandag coastal area.
1.1.3. Procuring and implementing of technology to trap litter from Asi river and collecting/separating marine litter in Samandag coastal area to be recycled and/or upcycled.
1.2.1. Preparing curriculum for Zero Waste Education in Early Childhood for SuTP and local communities
1.2.1.1. Recruiting a team of consultants on waste management, education programs, curriculumn development, pedagogic approach 
1.2.1.2. Assessing already present materials and the need for further materials with the MoEUCC and MoNE
1.2.2. Preparing Zero Waste Education Materials for Kids 
1.2.3. Preparing Training Materials for Mukhtars - head of villages 
1.2.4. Organization of trainings for mukhtars and training of trainers
1.2.4.1 Training Needs Assessment/Baseline Study 
2.1.1 Assessing the incentive mechanism ad deciding for the incentive mechanism for removal of plastic waste in Samandag
2.1.2 Procuring equipment for better removal of plastic waste from the sea
2.2. Development of a monitoring system to track invasion of water hyacinth in the Asi river and coastal area ecosystem 
2.2.1. Recruiting the consultant for the monitoring system development 
2.2.2. Development of the monitoring system development 
2.2.3. Implementation system for the monitoring system development 
2.3 Plowing or lifting the water hyacinth from the ground or from the periphery of river
2.2.1. Recruiting the consultant for water hyacinth 
2.2.2. Conducting the procurement for the removal after the method is identified 
3.1.1 Plastic Waste Assessment Report for Turkey 
3.1.2. Best Practices Report for Upcycling 
3.1.3. Guideline in dissemination of marine litter technology and innovation
3.1.4. Zero Waste Guidelines to Support Policy Implementation 
3.1.5. Energy Recovery Assessment Report</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Meeting with relevant stakeholders to intrdouce the project was completed, kick off meeting of the project was made in Hatay with the participation of stakeholders.
- Meetings were made with Japan organizations for possible know how between May and June 2022.
- RPA was signed with Nature Conservation Centre for the completion of outputs 1 and 2 of the project.
- IC recuritement procedures for Energy recovery assesment, best practices report for upcycling report is ongoing, IC recruitement process for Zero waste guidelines, plastic waste assesment report was completed and draft versions of the reports were completed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
